WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:08.250
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:14.760
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.590
It's my day!

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.170
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.580
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.950
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:49.360
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.130
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:02.270
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.780
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.920
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.990
I just want to walk

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.530
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.500
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:35.400
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:41.840
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.110
It's my day!

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.360
<i>It's starting.</i>

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.590
<i>My new relationship with Domyoji.</i>

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:36.070
"Time To Call It Quits"

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.780
<i>I want to see Domyoji soon.</i>

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:52.980
I want to see him!

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.850
<i>I want to go to him and find out...</i>

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.850
<i>what our new relationship will be like.</i>

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:45.770
<i>And yet...</i>

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:56.810
Good morning!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.980
Oh, Makino!

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.990
Say, where's Domyoji?

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.020
Who knows?
Haven't seen him this morning.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.190
He's probably sleeping in.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.530
You need him for something?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.500
Naw... just wanted to have a look
at his silly face. That's all.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.740
See ya!

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.220
<i>There's no hurry.
There's plenty of time.</i>

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:36.920
You want to drop out?

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:37.460
Yes.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.350
Forgive me for saying this,
but for someone like you...

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.730
there will probably never be
another chance to study abroad.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.730
But I've made my decision.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:46.930
Listen, Makino...

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.470
Principal's Office

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.670
Oh, and tell Domyoji's mom
that I'm no longer a concern.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:05.120
<i>I don't need to run away
from this school now.</i>

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.960
Well, now... if it isn't
our special exchange student...

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.290
I gave that up.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.330
No way!

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.000
<i>I don't hear their
hurtful words anymore.</i>

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.510
<i>Still... I'm getting tired
of waiting for him...</i>

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.010
Oh! You surprised me!

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.560
Makino, have you found Tsukasa?

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:45.560
No...

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:48.790
I guess he's playing hooky today.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.100
Too bad... I finally managed
to get tickets to that new club.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.870
Never mind.
If he's not here, he's not here.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.040
Makino, do you want to come?

00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.840
Of course not!

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.780
<i>Shigeru...</i>

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:09.550
<i>I told her clearly
that she wasn't the one.</i>

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.990
<i>Is it because she can't
give up on Domyoji?</i>

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:17.460
<i>But...</i>

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.030
Tsukushi!

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:26.960
Shigeru...

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.000
I went to pick Tsukasa up
this morning,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.070
but something was funny...

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.060
Funny? What was funny?

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.310
There were lots of men
standing around, like bodyguards.

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:39.510
This secretary, Nishida,
came out and said...

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.850
"Tsukasa will not be attending
school for a while."

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:45.580
When I asked why,
he kept giving vague answers.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.690
Hey, doesn't it sound
like something's up?

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.110
Yeah. It's not normal.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.990
<i>Why aren't you coming, Domyoji?</i>

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.770
Idiot

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.240
I want to see you.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.600
I want to see him...

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:07.610
I've <i>got</i> to see him!

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.500
Rui Hanazawa!

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.450
I'm coming with you.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.970
Looks like we're all
on the same wavelength.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.140
Nishikado!

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:44.180
Yup.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.110
You too, Mimasaka?

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.060
Shortcuts are a pain.

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.600
Shigeru!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.620
Tsubaki...
Why don't you sit down?

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.320
Mother...

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.520
How can you be so composed
after what you did to Tsukasa?

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:50.840
If I didn't do this...
he'd never understand his place.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.980
Mother... You can't control him
the way you did me.

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:58.320
He has changed.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.550
You should have realized that.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:03.550
Yes...

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:08.660
Tsukushi Makino...
She has ruined Tsukasa.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:15.670
At this rate, everything I've built up
will be destroyed.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.600
Mother...

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.450
<i>What a beautiful sky...</i>

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.920
Tsukasa! Where are you?

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:15.890
Tsukasa!

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:16.750
Answer us!

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.600
<i>Domyoji...</i>

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.130
Makino...

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.120
Huh?

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.250
Hmm?

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:53.730
Please come this way.
Mrs. Domyoji awaits you.

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:55.730
This way.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.560
Tsukushi!

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:15.550
Tsubaki...

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:19.680
Welcome, everyone.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:22.650
What, may I ask,
are you all doing here?

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.180
We heard that Tsukasa
wasn't coming to school...

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:38.140
so we decided to come here
and find out why.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:43.940
Shigeru...

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.810
You needn't worry at all
about Tsukasa.

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:53.580
It's really nothing at all.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:01.390
And so, I would like you all
to leave now.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.700
Are you afraid?

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:14.040
To see Domyoji changing...

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.710
What could you be talking about?

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.150
Tsukasa is my son.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.350
I have nothing to fear from him.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:28.350
Is that so?

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:40.160
I found myself in a completely
different world at Eitoku.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.850
Domyoji and I did nothing but fight...

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:07.960
But in the end,
he always came to my rescue.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:19.670
And yet...

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:27.550
I did my best not to accept him
because he was not of my world.

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:37.190
Last night, he told me...

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:41.590
that the stewed potatoes
my mother made were delicious.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:45.460
Tsukasa...

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.140
And what should I make of that?

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.870
Domyoji tried to understand that...

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:09.420
...in the world of common people...
the world that you despise...

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:12.990
there are lots of wonderful things
that money can't buy.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:16.260
When I realized that...

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:20.370
I was finally able
to accept his feelings.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.270
You...

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:33.850
You're probably afraid that
the day will come...

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:40.490
when he will no longer need
your world... or you.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.370
Being young
is a wonderful thing, but...

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.770
The young make many mistakes.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:06.340
Tsukasa's feelings for you
are temporary.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:11.350
When he matures, he will see
that you are unworthy of him.

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:13.850
Mother, what are you saying?!

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.390
Unworthy?

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.090
Perhaps you're right...

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:27.600
But he is the one who should be
allowed to realize that.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.600
You can't force it on him.

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:39.480
Is that all you have to say?

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:51.660
If they took the Domyoji "brand"
away from you...

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:56.560
there would probably
be nothing left.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:16:59.730
I pity you.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:32.660
I want to see him.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:48.950
Domyoji!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.620
Makino, I...

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.070
Why did you do that?

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:53.140
I told you...
that I'd leap into your world.

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:06.860
You know...

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:10.800
This morning, I played hopscotch
for the first time in years.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:18.340
It was fun. I thought something new
was starting today.

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:29.180
But...

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:52.470
If things like this continue,
neither you, nor I, will last.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:56.410
And so...

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.910
It's time to call it quits.

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:02.350
Makino...

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:05.320
Thank you, Domyoji.

00:20:53.970 --> 00:20:54.870
Tsukushi!

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:57.300
Is this what you want, Tsukasa?

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.240
Go after her, Tsukasa!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:06.530
Tsukasa, hurry!

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.080
Tsukushi... Tsukushi is leaving!

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:20.330
I finally understand how you felt.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:26.960
Tsukasa...

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:38.840
Good-bye, Tsukasa.
Say good-bye to your heroine...

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.020
Tsukushi Makino...

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:04.680
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:09.430
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:18.900
Some day, the whole world

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:24.710
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:32.460
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:38.080
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:44.700
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:51.100
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:58.000
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:06.880
Let's keep running down
 the road we believe in!

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:14.790
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:20.850
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:28.110
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:31.500
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:37.370
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:49.840
Domyoji and Shigeru
didn't come back to school.

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:54.050
I got a 50-yen raise
at my part-time job.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:58.150
I'm back to my peaceful,
unexciting life.

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:00.550
Good-bye, heroine...

00:24:00.890 --> 00:24:04.520
I guess this is the life
I've been hoping for.

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:08.130
Hana Yori Dango: "Neverending"
